      "turn": 1,
      "user": "I need the wall ready for finishing quickly. How does block installation compare with cast-in-situ curing?",
      "assistant": "When looking to finish your walls quickly, pre-cast hemp-lime blocks are generally favored for speed because they arrive already cured. Once they are laid with lime mortar, you typically only need a short planning window of about 2 to 3 days for the mortar to set before you can move on to the plaster sequencing. \n\nIn contrast, cast-in-situ hemp-lime is tamped directly into forms on-site. While the forms can often be removed the next day, the material itself requires a natural curing period of about 3 to 6 weeks before you can apply the final plaster, depending on drying conditions. Because final structural, code, and permit decisions depend on your local jurisdiction and a qualified professional, it is always wise to consult a local expert for your specific build.\n\nWhat installation method are you leaning toward for your project?"
    }
